00:18:01,595 --> 00:18:07,115
the rigging. It's a ticklish business, but it must be done or else it's no go.

211
00:18:07,116 --> 00:18:11,914
But none of us are in heaven yet. Drop your tongs, cook, and hear my orders. Do

212
00:18:11,915 --> 00:18:18,079
you hear? Hold your hat in one hand and clap the other a top your heart when I'm

213
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:24,399
giving my orders. Cook. What? That your heart there? That's your gizzard. A

214
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:31,594
loft. A loft. That's it. Now you have it. Hold it there now and pay attention.

215
00:18:31,595 --> 00:18:37,115
all attention," said the old black, with both hands placed as desired, vainly

216
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:41,999
wriggling his grizzled head as if to get both ears in front at one in the same

217
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:48,399
time. "Well, then, cook, you see this whale steak of yours was so very bad

218
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:53,914
that I have put it out of sight as soon as possible. You see that, don't you?

219
00:18:53,915 --> 00:18:58,159
Well, for the future, when you cook another whale steak for my private table

220
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:04,638
here, the capston, I'll tell you what to do so as not to spoil it by overdoing.

221
00:19:04,639 --> 00:19:09,838
Hold the steak in one hand and show a live coal to it with the other. That

222
00:19:09,839 --> 00:19:14,878
done, dish it. Do you hear? And now, tomorrow, cook, when we are cutting in

223
00:19:14,879 --> 00:19:20,079
